V_025 chain: base V_034, then 107 + 136 + 136 + 136 body blocks (kick and two-mode tom at transcribed kick, tom, snare and clap hits), 3 x 80 gap blocks (kick, tom or burst at the strongest deficits away from transcribed hits), one bed table 28 bands x 202 eighth notes, one segment EQ table of the same size, two class tables (6 classes x 6 then 9 nodes). Total about 835 blocks and about 12 000 table cells for 68 s of audio. (12 October 2026)

## 5. Honest limits (12 October 2026)

The score is magnitude only (46 ms frames); the stem has not been checked by ear, and the verdict belongs to Matthieu. The model is heavily parameterised: the bed and segment EQ tables are coarse (eighth notes, about 7 critic frames per cell, deliberately not finer, so they stay a dynamic EQ and noise bed rather than a vocoder of the reference), but the blocks are fitted greedily on the very measure they are scored by, so part of the gain is fitting rather than transcription; plossBarNoOnset and plossEvents, which the fit never sees, also rise (+3.6 and +3.1), which suggests the gain is not only overfitting. Gap blocks sit at times where the score has no hit: they are a measured hint that the drum transcription still misses events (onsetF 0.903). (12 October 2026)

